# Note @NOTE_VERSION@ release notes

Release date: not set. This is a release candidate built for testing.

Note is a lightweight, file-oriented text editor for Windows.

## Install

1. Check the download against its checksum:
   `Get-FileHash Note-@NOTE_VERSION@-windows-x64.zip -Algorithm SHA256`
   The hash must match `Note-@NOTE_VERSION@-windows-x64.zip.sha256`.
2. Unzip anywhere and run `note.exe`. No installer or extra runtime is needed.

Settings, themes, session and recovery data are stored per user in `%APPDATA%\Note`.

## Included

- Plain-text editing with multiple tabs and cursors, undo/redo, smart indentation and bracket/quote pairing.
- Find and replace with case, whole-word and regular-expression options.
- Themes and a theme editor, typography, layout, editing preferences and configurable shortcuts.
- Command palette, menus, context menus and keyboard navigation.
- Encoding and line-ending preservation, atomic saves and external-change detection.
- Session restore and crash recovery of unsaved text.
- Open the current file in another application, or a terminal in its folder.

Syntax highlighting and language detection are not part of this release.

## Known limitations

- Tested only on Windows 11 (x64). Windows 10 is untested.
- Typing and opening large files miss the provisional performance targets on the 4 GB test laptop; see `docs/PERFORMANCE.md` in the source.
- Large files are shown only after they are fully loaded.
- The editor text is not exposed to screen readers.
- If Note is killed while saving, a temporary file such as `name.txt.AbCdEf` may remain beside the original. The original file stays complete.
- Not yet checked by hand on a real display: native dialogs, drag and drop from Explorer, and external app or terminal launches.

